      "writtenOn": "2026-08-05T07:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since SoftwareIdentifier currently relies on a uint16_t for the component ID, using any magic number (whether 0 or 0xFFFF) carries a theoretical risk of collision if a vendor uses that specific ID.\nWould you recommend keeping 0xFFFF as a approach since it is less likely to be used than 0, or should we consider expanding SoftwareIdentifier (e.g., adding an image_level flag) in a separate commit to fix the root cause completely?",
      "parentUuid": "fe8d7ccb_1c0d6419",
